The app commands that exist on this entry are `where`, `validate`, `test-run`, `bridge-test`, `bridge-status`, `bridge-recover`, `clerk-deliver`, `pack-check`, `pack-preview`, `pack-assemble`, `pack-verify`, `prime-status`, `boot-prepare`, `boot-check`, `boot-judge`, `boot-show`, and `batch-observe`. `run` stays refused. The cold exercise permits three read-only calls, and no others:

```text
python -B app/librarian.py batch-observe --repo D:/Git/lib-build --commit c1a11dc9014eed37506f19aba7d41e3ca3213106 --path 00.kernel/00.00.10.work/0508.return-capture/05.16.md --json
python -B labs/return-capture-pass01/return_inspect.py inspect --book D:/Git/lib-build/00.kernel/00.00.10.work --member 0144.batch-reader-entry-0516 --json
python -B app/librarian.py boot-show --attempt <external-attempt-directory> --json
```

`boot-show` is permitted only after the Director has run prepare into an external records directory and has handed that path over. `boot-prepare`, `boot-check`, and `boot-judge` write attempt files. The model does not run them. `prime-status` is accepted and stays out of this exercise because the packet names no registry. Pack assemble, clerk deliver, bridge, and test-run stay out because they write or execute.

The boot tool's own caps, from `prime_boot.py`, are 12 refs and 131072 bytes. A request may set lower limits. It may not set higher ones. Overflow is an omission record. Required evidence is not silently truncated.

