## What a sealed boot packet still needs

A final packet, when Prime later seals it, carries these parts:

- Role, from R08: Director, Codex Prime, and Claude Colab stay as recorded. Per-pack executors are already valid. This exercise label "Prime" is the fresh model under test. It does not replace the standing Prime.
- Declared scope: the eleven paths above, plus the external attempt's status scope once prepare has run. Attention order is advice. It does not decide O1.
- Explicit current-work source: R01. It names `0504.app-entry/05.06.md`. That page is 13597 bytes at the same commit, SHA-256 `a9ee40b19dd6af021df32e5a89a344ca829146dd9a9b9a6a8f88bffbe8c7f4fc`, and it is not a packet ref. The model must not reconstruct it from memory.
- Brief with raw evidence links: the twelfth ref. It is pending. See the dependency section.
- Pending, held, and accepted distinctions: R03, R04, R05, R07, and R11. A bound review with `terminal: completed` is the projection's completion rule. Review text alone does not complete a batch. A receipt does not publish a package.
- Unresolved Director decisions: R02 items D1, D2, D3, and D4. D1 is the stale canonical assignment against parallel lanes. This plan does not invent a new authority and does not declare a highest-page winner.
- Exact tool instructions: the three commands in this plan, R09, and R10.

R01 and R02 together are the canonical-assignment conflict. O1 must be able to acknowledge it. Electing `05.06` as the only current work, or electing a later lane because it is newer, are both outside this plan.

